<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdallah al-Ghalib</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1517">1517</a>–<a href="/years/1574">1574</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdallah al-Ghalib was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from 1557 to 1574, the son and successor of Muhammad al-Shaykh in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saadi-dynasty">Saadi dynasty</a>. He defeated an Ottoman army from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> at Wadi al-Laban near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> in 1558 and kept Morocco independent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a> he rebuilt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ben-youssef-madrasa">Ben Youssef Madrasa</a> and built the Mouassine Mosque.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdallah-al-ghalib.jpg" alt="Abdallah al-Ghalib" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michal Osmenda from Brussels, Belgium · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marrakesh,_Ben_Youssef_Medersa_(5365345360)_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
